  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through Tuesday)\nIssued at 144 PM CST Wed Nov 18 2026\n\nFriday and Saturday will be the warmest days of the extended \nforecast as temperatures continue to gradually move into the upper \n60s to low 70s nearly areawide. However, the pattern changes heading \ninto Saturday evening as an upper low swings out of the Rockies and \ninto the Great Plains. A cold front moves through the region \nSaturday evening and temperatures fall into the 40s for Sunday \nmorning. Highs from Sunday through Tuesday will struggle to reach \nout of the 50s for many locations. Long range guidance also has a \nweak disturbance crossing the area late Monday into Tuesday and \nbringing low(10-30%) chances for rain across the northern half of \nthe CWA. Rain chances disappear after Tuesday. \n\n-Stickney",
